title: Genesis 7 – The Flood
description: A study in Genesis 7: the Flood, God’s judgment on the wicked and the scoffers, and just Noah saved by faith.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-7-the-flood.html

=== Introduction
--- The Flood [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 7
sub: God’s judgment on the wicked and the scoffers, and just Noah saved by faith.
refs: Genesis 7:1-5
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== Into the ark
--- Come thou and all thy house
heading: “Come thou and all thy house”
scripture: Genesis 7:1-5 | mark: thee have I seen righteous
- God calls Noah in: “for thee have I seen righteous before me in this generation.” Just Noah, who found grace in the eyes of the {Lord}. [[Genesis 6:8-9]]
- Seven days of warning, then forty days and forty nights of rain.
- “And Noah did according unto all that the {Lord} commanded him.” Faith obeys.

--- Eight souls
scripture: Genesis 7:13-15
stat: 8 | souls: Noah, his wife, his three sons and their wives
stat: 7 | days after God called them in, the waters came
stat: 1 | ark, and one door
center: “Wherein few, that is, eight souls were saved by water.” [[1 Peter 3:20]]

--- And the Lord shut him in [title]
overline: Genesis 7:16
heading: And the {Lord} shut him in
center: Noah built the ark, but God closed the door. Those inside were kept by the {Lord}, and those outside were not let in. [[Genesis 7:16]]

=== The judgment
--- Windows of heaven, fountains of the deep
big: Genesis 7:11-12 | mark: fountains of the great deep; windows of heaven
center: Waters pouring in from the skies like through open windows, and up from the deep like a fountain.

--- The waters prevailed
scripture: Genesis 7:17-20 | mark: all the high hills, that were under the whole heaven, were covered
stat: 40 | days and nights of rain
stat: 15 | cubits above the highest mountains
stat: 150 | days the waters prevailed upon the earth
note: “All the high hills, that were under the whole heaven, were covered.” A global flood. [[Genesis 7:24]]

--- All flesh died
scripture: Genesis 7:21-23 | mark: Noah only remained alive
p: God’s judgment came upon the wicked and the scoffers, and the corrupt earth tainted with the blood of violence and sin. All flesh died, and just Noah was saved, with his sons and their wives, along with the animals of the earth. [[Genesis 6:11-13]]

=== This is true
--- The Bible says it’s true
lead: There are archeologies and secular histories that all confirm a global flood, relegated to “myth” status but wondered about by natural men, seeking to confirm the story by natural means.
panel: The face of the earth | Fossils of sea life found on top of Everest, and deposits of salt in high plateaus. The deluge changing the face of the earth in grand canyons and fiords and river beds.
panel: One family of man | The common descent of every nation of men, traced back to the sons of Noah. [[Genesis 9:18-19|Gen 9:19]] [[Acts 17:26]]
callout: **But the Bible says it’s true, and that’s enough.** The science of man comes around to confirming the accounts of scripture, not the other way around.

--- Willingly ignorant
big: 2 Peter 3:3-6 | mark: willingly
p: Scoffers laugh at the idea of Biblical fundamentalism, and some believers take it personally and are embarrassed by the word of God. We shouldn’t be moved. Rather, those scoffers should be embarrassed by themselves and their own foolish hearts.

=== Ready with an answer
--- Ready always to give an answer
scripture: 1 Peter 3:13-17 | mark: be ready always to give an answer
- Be not afraid of their terror, neither be troubled.
- Sanctify the Lord God in your hearts, and answer with meekness and fear.
- Keep a good conscience, that they who speak evil of you may be ashamed.

--- Eight souls were saved by water
scripture: 1 Peter 3:18-21 | mark: eight souls were saved by water
panel: Christ in triumph | Jesus was triumphantly shown in Hell before those that didn’t believe, preaching His glory, leading captivity captive. [[Ephesians 4:8-9]]
panel-warn: The disobedient | The scoffers and unbelievers who mocked God, while the longsuffering of God waited, were swallowed up in the flood.

=== The Lord delivers
--- The Lord knoweth how to deliver the godly
heading: The {Lord} knoweth how to deliver
scripture: 2 Peter 2:4-9 | mark: saved Noah the eighth person, a preacher of righteousness
panel: Noah | A preacher of righteousness, saved with his house while the world of the ungodly was destroyed.
panel: Lot | Just Lot, vexed by the filthy conversation of the wicked, delivered before the fire fell on Sodom and Gomorrha.

--- The faith of Noah
big: Hebrews 11:7
p: We are called to have the faith of Noah, who, having the grace of God extended to him, and faith in the Christ to come, believed God’s promise of salvation. Building the ark, diligently and meekly, obeying the {Lord}. Vexed, like Lot, by the sinful fallen world around him. Yet Noah stayed true, and God delivered him and destroyed the wicked, just as He will in the great day of the {Lord}.
refs: Matthew 24:37-39

=== Close
--- Stand ready [title]
overline: Genesis 7
sub: by faith in God’s word, like Noah.
point: The judgment was real | A global flood upon a corrupt and violent world. The Bible says it’s true, and that’s enough.
point: The ark was God’s provision | One ark, one door, and the {Lord} shut him in. Eight souls were saved by water.
point: Have an answer | Stand ready with an answer for our hope, meekly and with fear, standfast in the truth.
point: He delivers, and He judges | God rewards those who diligently seek Him, and, despite all longsuffering, delivers His wrath on the wicked. [[Hebrews 11:6]]
